-- title:
--   Definition 17 — the commutant of a representation is the set of operators commuting with every $U_g$
-- statement:
--   Let $U$ be a representation of a group $G$ on $H$, and let $\mathcal A$ be the algebra generated by $\{U_g:g\in G\}$. An operator $T$ on $H$ lies in the commutant $\mathcal C(\mathcal A)$ if and only if
--   $$
--   T\,U_g=U_g\,T\qquad\text{for all } g\in G.
--   $$
--   This is what makes $\mathcal C(U)$ the set of operators commuting with the representation, the form in which it is used in the source.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - reading: the commutant of the algebra generated by U; the pointwise form is used without a statement → T ∈ C(A) iff T commutes with each U_g; reason: the source passes between the two without comment (p.25: "the set of all operators commuting with a representation")
--   - generalization: a unitary representation on a Hilbert space, over ℂ → any representation of a group on a vector space over a field; reason: unitarity and the inner product play no part; the source case specializes
-- source:
--   Ragone et al., Representation Theory for Geometric Quantum Machine Learning, arXiv:2210.07980v2, Definition 17 and the sentence before it, p.28

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_RepGQML_commutant
import Definitions.Def_RepGQML_groupAlgebra

namespace RepGQML

/-- The commutant of the algebra generated by the representatives is the set of operators commuting
with every `U_g` (Ragone et al., *Representation Theory for Geometric Quantum Machine Learning*, arXiv:2210.07980v2, Definition 17 and the sentence before it, p.28). -/
theorem mem_commutant_groupAlgebra_iff {k G H : Type*} [Field k] [Group G] [AddCommGroup H]
    [Module k H] (U : Representation k G H) (T : Module.End k H) :
    T ∈ commutant (groupAlgebra U) ↔ ∀ g : G, T * U g = U g * T := by sorry

end RepGQML
